{"id":"2f4aaf7e7caa9eb91fb6abefc05a78a899698b5b","axis":"silent","repo":"aquasecurity/trivy","sha":"2f4aaf7e7caa9eb91fb6abefc05a78a899698b5b","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/guide/scanner/crypto.md","lines":["@@ -18,9 +18,11 @@ Trivy rejects `--scanners crypto` with other report formats."," "," Files are selected by extension: `.pem`, `.der`, `.crt`, `.cer`, `.key`. The encoding comes from the content, since these extensions carry both PEM and DER."," ","+Keystores are selected by the `.p12`, `.pfx`, `.jks` and `.keystore` extensions and by the exact file name `cacerts` of the Java trust store. A `.jks` file is read when it holds PKCS#12, which keytool writes by default since JDK 9.","+"," | Material | Formats |"," | --- | --- |","-| X.509 certificates | PEM, DER |","+| X.509 certificates | PEM, DER, PKCS#12 keystores |"," | Private keys | PKCS#1, PKCS#8, SEC1, in PEM or DER |"," | Public keys | PKIX, in PEM or DER |"," | Encrypted private keys | PKCS#8 in PEM or DER, legacy encrypted PEM |","@@ -183,7 +185,7 @@ The scanner is available for `trivy image` only."," "," Trivy rejects `--scanners crypto` together with [`--sbom-sources`](../target/container_image.md#discover-sbom-referencing-the-container-image), because a remote SBOM found for the image replaces the analysis of its layers."," ","-A file without one of the extensions above is not read, so a key in a file named `tls-key` or inside a config file is missed. You can point the scanner at such a file with [`--file-patterns`](../configuration/skipping.md#customizing-file-handling), as long as it holds PEM or DER material:","+A file without one of the extensions above is not read, so a key in a file named `tls-key` or inside a config file is missed. You can point the scanner at such a file with [`--file-patterns`](../configuration/skipping.md#customizing-file-handling), as long as it holds PEM or DER material or a PKCS#12 keystore:"," "," ```shell"," $ trivy image --scanners crypto --format cyclonedx --file-patterns \"crypto:etc/app/tls-key\" myimage:1.0.0","@@ -191,4 +193,8 @@ $ trivy image --scanners crypto --format cyclonedx --file-patterns \"crypto:etc/a"," "," Files larger than 10 MB are skipped, because a file of that size with one of these extensions is almost never cryptographic material."," ","-Some objects are recognized and skipped. Certificate signing requests, CRLs and PKCS#7 bundles are not part of the inventory. OpenSSH keys, PKCS#12 and JKS keystores and OpenPGP keyrings are not covered yet. A certificate or key that uses an EC key with explicit curve parameters instead of a named curve cannot be parsed and is skipped as well. Private keys of X25519, X448 and Ed448 are skipped, although their public keys are reported.","+Some objects are recognized and skipped. Certificate signing requests, CRLs and PKCS#7 bundles are not part of the inventory. OpenSSH keys, JKS and JCEKS keystores and OpenPGP keyrings are not covered yet. A certificate or key that uses an EC key with explicit curve parameters instead of a named curve cannot be parsed and is skipped as well. Private keys of X25519, X448 and Ed448 are skipped, although their public keys are reported.","+","+Trivy does not decrypt PKCS#12 keystores and does not report their private keys, so it reads only the certificates stored without encryption. keytool, OpenSSL and .NET encrypt the certificates unless encryption is turned off explicitly, such as with `-certpbe NONE` in OpenSSL or `-J-Dkeystore.pkcs12.certProtectionAlgorithm=NONE` in keytool. OpenSSL encrypts them even with an empty password. The `cacerts` trust store that ships with JDK 18 and later has no password and is read in full.","+","+The `cacerts` of JDK 17 and earlier is a JKS keystore and is skipped. A PKCS#12 keystore protected by a public-key signature instead of a password-based MAC is not read. Parts of a keystore encoded in BER rather than DER are skipped. Trivy reads at most 10000 bags from one keystore."],"additions":9,"deletions":3,"tru